$ jailops app install postgresql --name db --image freebsd-151@stable
App postgresql installed as jail db (running)
  Version:   18.6
  Addresses: 10.20.0.10
  Ports:     postgres 5432/tcp at 10.20.0.10:5432 The SQL port.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow db from SOURCE
  Data:      /var/db/postgres The cluster (data18).
  Config:    /var/db/postgres/data18/postgresql.conf (restart postgresql) Server settings.
             /var/db/postgres/data18/pg_hba.conf (restart postgresql) Who may connect.
  Logs:      server /var/log/messages The port logs to syslog.
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback db --all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     12 done
Notes:
  Connect from inside the jail with: jailops exec NAME -- su -l postgres -c psql

$ jailops app install nginx --name web --image freebsd-151@stable
App nginx installed as jail web (running)
  Version:   1.30.6,3
  Addresses: 10.20.0.11
  Ports:     http 80/tcp at 10.20.0.11:80 (expose: forwarding is not set up yet) HTTP, the default site.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow web from SOURCE
  Data:      /usr/local/www The sites.
  Config:    /usr/local/etc/nginx/nginx.conf (restart nginx) The server configuration.
  Logs:      access /var/log/nginx/access.log One line per request.
             error /var/log/nginx/error.log
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback web --all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     10 done
Notes:
  Put the site under /usr/local/www.

$ jailops firewall address-set create postgresql_allow --address @web --comment the web jail
address set/postgresql_allow created

$ jailops firewall policy create postgres --rule allow in tcp from @postgresql_allow port 5432 comment who may reach PostgreSQL
firewall policy/postgres created

$ jailops config set db firewall.policies postgres
jail/db configuration updated

$ jailops firewall test --from @web --to @db --port 5432
tcp port 5432 10.20.0.11 -> 10.20.0.10 (inet)
  out of web (jailops/main/web, epair in): PASS by the default of the anchor
      pass in quick all (fake default)
  into db (jailops/main/db, gateway out): PASS by policy postgres rule 1 "who may reach PostgreSQL"
      pass out quick (fake rule)
  Verdict: PASS

Not covered:
  - the answer is for a new connection: a connection that is already open (pf keeps its state) is not asked about

$ jailops firewall test --from @web --to @db --port 5433
tcp port 5433 10.20.0.11 -> 10.20.0.10 (inet)
  out of web (jailops/main/web, epair in): PASS by the default of the anchor
      pass in quick all (fake default)
  into db (jailops/main/db, gateway out): BLOCK by the default of the anchor
      block drop out quick all (fake default)
  Verdict: BLOCK

Not covered:
  - the answer is for a new connection: a connection that is already open (pf keeps its state) is not asked about
[exit 1]

$ jailops firewall test --from @web --to @db --proto icmp
icmp echoreq 10.20.0.11 -> 10.20.0.10 (inet)
  out of web (jailops/main/web, epair in): PASS by the default of the anchor
      pass in quick all (fake default)
  into db (jailops/main/db, gateway out): BLOCK by the default of the anchor
      block drop out quick all (fake default)
  Verdict: BLOCK

Not covered:
  - no ICMP type was given: the test is an echo request (ping); other types may meet other rules
  - the answer is for a new connection: a connection that is already open (pf keeps its state) is not asked about
[exit 1]

$ jailops firewall test --from @web --to @db --port 5432 -o json
{
  "verdict": "pass",
  "cases": [
    {
      "family": "inet",
      "from": "10.20.0.11",
      "to": "10.20.0.10",
      "proto": "tcp",
      "port": 5432,
      "verdict": "pass",
      "hops": [
        {
          "side": "source",
          "jail": "web",
          "anchor": "jailops/main/web",
          "interface": "epair",
          "direction": "in",
          "verdict": "pass",
          "decided_by": {
            "stage": "default",
            "pf": "pass in quick all (fake default)"
          }
        },
        {
          "side": "destination",
          "jail": "db",
          "anchor": "jailops/main/db",
          "interface": "gateway",
          "direction": "out",
          "verdict": "pass",
          "decided_by": {
            "stage": "policy",
            "policy": "postgres",
            "rule": 1,
            "comment": "who may reach PostgreSQL",
            "pf": "pass out quick (fake rule)"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "the answer is for a new connection: a connection that is already open (pf keeps its state) is not asked about"
  ]
}

$ jailops firewall test --to @db --port 5432
! usage: --from and --to are required
! hint: run 'jailops firewall test --help' for usage
[exit 2]

$ jailops firewall test --from @web --to @db
! invalid: a tcp test needs a port from 1 to 65535
[exit 2]

$ jailops firewall test --from @web --to @nobody --port 5432
! not_found: jail "nobody" not found
! hint: list them with 'jailops jail list'; check --project, --host and --remote too
[exit 4]

